==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|treat with kid gloves}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|kid glove}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-handle with kid gloves.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*|head=[[handle]] [[with]] [[kid glove]]s}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To treat something very [[delicately]] or [[carefully]].
#: {{ux|en|The campaign staff cautioned the candidate to '''handle''' the issue '''with kid gloves'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/politics/2003/aug/03/israelandthepalestinians.pressandpublishing|author=Stephen Pritchard|title=Racist or just anti-Sharon?|date=2003-08-03|work=The Guardian|passage=[Richard] Ingrams has always enjoyed a reputation for insensitivity. As with other columnists in the British press, he treads on toes to make his point and rides roughshod over issues that others '''handle with kid gloves''', or avoid altogether.}}

